idence: excellent attention skills (addresses numeric handling), calm in crisis, quick correct decisions, concern for others (crew cooperation), and technical competence (understands complicated technology). While communication difficulty and egocentric are concerns, they may be mitigated.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 argued D is best due to concentration and memory, but we can say that C's excellent attention skills also address numeric handling, and his concern for others offsets his communication issues. Also, D's arrogance and weak leadership may be more detrimental to crew dynamics than C's communication difficulty.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe must ensure we use explicit facts: C has excellent attention skills, keeps calm in a crisis, can make correct decisions quickly, puts concern for others above everything, understands complicated technology. Also note his difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric. D's arrogance, weak leadership, moody, loner.\n\nWe'll argue that C's strengths align with criteria and his cooperation concerns are less severe than D's arrogance.\n\nThus final vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
